cosm-public ipxe readme

## Usage

Set up iPXE boot menu

cd ~/ipxe/src
nano embed.ipxe

# embed.ipxe for pxe boot:
```
#!ipxe
dhcp && goto netboot || goto dhcperror

:dhcperror
prompt --key s --timeout 10000 DHCP failed, hit 's' for the iPXE shell; reboot in 10 seconds && shell || reboot

:netboot
chain tftp://${next-server}/main.ipxe ||
prompt --key s --timeout 10000 Chainloading failed, hit 's' for the iPXE shell; reboot in 10 seconds && shell || reboot
```

# embed.ipxe for http boot:

```
#!ipxe
dhcp && goto netboot || goto dhcperror

:dhcperror
prompt --key s --timeout 10000 DHCP failed, hit 's' for the iPXE shell; reboot in 10 seconds && shell || reboot

:netboot
chain http://10.30.112.98/main.ipxe ||
prompt --key s --timeout 10000 Chainloading failed, hit 's' for the iPXE shell; reboot in 10 seconds && shell || reboot
```

# Add ping and ntfs support to ipxe

cd ~/ipxe/src
# NTFS support
sed -i 's/#undef\tDOWNLOAD_PROTO_NFS/#define\tDOWNLOAD_PROTO_NFS/' config/general.h

# Ping support
sed -i 's/\/\/#define\ PING_CMD/#define\ PING_CMD/' config/general.h
sed -i 's/\/\/#define\ IPSTAT_CMD/#define\ IPSTAT_CMD/' config/general.h
sed -i 's/\/\/#define\ REBOOT_CMD/#define\ REBOOT_CMD/' config/general.h
sed -i 's/\/\/#define\ POWEROFF/#define\ POWEROFF/' config/general.h

# Build ipxe
cd ~/ipxe/src
make bin-x86_64-efi/ipxe.efi EMBED=embed.ipxe

# Copy ipxe network boot firmware

- Note: This should be served via TFTP or HTTP (TFTP for ipxe boot, NGINX for HTTP boot)

```
cp ~/ipxe/src/bin-x86_64-efi/ipxe.efi /pxe-boot/ipxe.efi
```

# Hello workld iPXE Menu
nano /pxe-boot/main.ipxe

```
#!ipxe
:MENU
menu
item --gap -- ---------------- iPXE boot menu ----------------
item hello        Hello world
item shell          ipxe shell
choose --default return --timeout 5000 target && goto ${target}

:hello
echo "hello world"
boot ||
goto MENU

:shell
shell ||
goto MENU

autoboot
```

# Additional Resources:
- https://github.com/ipxe/wimboot -> Wimboot is fast way to boot into windows pe using HTTP
- https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-hardware/manufacture/desktop/winpe-create-usb-bootable-drive?view=windows-11 --> Creating WINPE wim file
- https://www.dell.com/support/home/en-us?app=drivers -> Drivers for Dell needed for WinPE to access drives and networking
- https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-hardware/manufacture/desktop/add-and-remove-drivers-to-an-offline-windows-image?view=windows-11 -> Adding drivers to WIM files
- https://ipxe.org/ -> Reference for ipxe related documentation, error codes, and writing ipxe scripts


